/* settings: label left, control right, the explanation as a quiet line under it */
#stt-form dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(200px,300px) minmax(0,1fr);margin:8px 0 0;background:var(--stt-box)}
#stt-form dl dt,#stt-form dl dd{float:none;width:auto;margin:0;padding:9px 12px;border-top:1px solid var(--stt-line);text-align:left;line-height:1.5}
#stt-form dl dt{opacity:.75;font-weight:normal}
#stt-form dl dt:first-child,#stt-form dl dt:first-child+dd{border-top:0}
/* Unraid 7 lays every dd out as a flex column (default-base.css, dl > dd): here one setting = one wrapping row */
#stt-form dl dd{display:flex;flex-direction:row;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:6px 8px}
#stt-form dl dd>.stt-hint,#stt-form dl dd>.stt-brk,#stt-form dl dd>div{flex:1 1 100%}
#stt-form dl dd>.stt-brk{height:0}
#stt-form dd input,#stt-form dd select,#stt-form dd textarea{margin:0;max-width:100%}
#stt-form dd select{width:auto!important;min-width:110px}
#stt-form dd input.narrow{width:80px!important;min-width:0}
#stt-form dd input[type=checkbox]{width:auto!important;margin:0 4px 0 0}
#stt-form dd label{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;margin-right:12px}
#stt .stt-lead .stt-leadact{flex:1 1 100%}
#stt .stt-hint{display:block;opacity:.55;font-size:12px;margin-top:3px;max-width:110ch}
@media (max-width:760px){#stt-form dl{grid-template-columns:1fr}#stt-form dl dd{border-top:0;padding-top:0}}
</style>
<div id="stt">
<div class="stt-title"><h2>Seedbox Tools</h2><span class="stt-mut">Only scans run by themselves. Nothing is added, replaced or deleted without your click.</span></div>
<nav class="stt-nav"><a href="#stt-t-find">Find my torrent <i id="stt-n-find"></i></a><a href="#stt-t-upd">Shape up <i id="stt-n-upd"></i></a><a href="#stt-t-rep">Season repacker <i id="stt-n-rep"></i></a><a href="#stt-t-set">Settings</a></nav>
<details class="stt-about"><summary class="stt-mut">What do the tools do?</summary>
<p>A seedbox, or a media server that seeds, only does its job if it seeds as many of its media files as possible. Content that nothing seeds is wasted: the ratio does not grow and the trackers may even drop you. The three tools work with Prowlarr, Radarr, Sonarr and qBittorrent.</p>
<p><b>Find my torrent</b> looks for torrents (through Prowlarr) for the files in your downloads folders that nothing is seeding. <b>Shape up</b> (formerly Update me) searches every big, old, seeded title in the background and offers a smaller release, a better HDR format or a higher resolution, replaced through Radarr or Sonarr after you approve. <b>Season repacker</b> replaces the single episodes of a finished season with the season pack, so that one torrent seeds the whole season (the torrents it adds get the <code>seasonrepacker</code> tag); it can also watch autobrr for new season packs.</p>
</details>

<div class="mt-band"><span>Activity</span><b>replacements and added torrents</b></div>
<div class="stt-sec stt-s-proc" id="stt-proc" style="display:none"></div>
<div class="stt-sec stt-s-res" id="stt-results"><div class="stt-sh">Results</div><p class="stt-mut" style="margin:8px 10px">Nothing finished yet.</p></div>

<div class="mt-band" id="stt-t-find"><span>Find my torrent</span><b id="stt-fband"></b></div>
<div class="mt-box">
<div class="stt-lead"><p>Folders in the downloads folders that no torrent seeds: the original torrent is looked up on the trackers, or the content can be replaced.</p><input type="button" id="stt-fscan" value="Scan the downloads folders"></div>
<div class="stt-status" id="stt-fstat"><span id="stt-fmsg"></span><span id="stt-queue"></span></div>
</div>
<div class="mt-box stt-flist"><div id="stt-fitems"></div></div>

<div class="mt-band" id="stt-t-upd"><span>Shape up</span><b id="stt-uband"></b></div>
<div class="mt-box">
<div class="stt-lead"><p>Every listed torrent is searched in the background, one about every 90 seconds, a result is kept for 10 days. Offered: a release smaller by the saving, a better HDR format (SDR, HDR, DV) or a higher resolution, never a lower one. Hungarian audio comes first but is not required.</p><input type="button" id="stt-uscan" value="Scan the seeded torrents"></div>
<div class="stt-status"><span id="stt-umsg"></span><div id="stt-ubg"></div></div>
<div class="stt-filter" id="stt-ubar" style="display:none"><input type="text" id="stt-uq" placeholder="filter by name" autocomplete="off"> <span id="stt-ucats"></span></div>
</div>
<div class="mt-box stt-ulist"><div id="stt-uitems"></div></div>
<p class="stt-foot">The scan matches the file sizes of your torrents with the files in Radarr and Sonarr; a torrent with several seasons is listed but not supported yet. Radarr and Sonarr decide whether a chosen release is an upgrade: if it waits with &ldquo;Not an upgrade&rdquo;, import it by hand in Activity, Queue. After the import the old torrent and its files can be removed here with one more click.</p>

<div class="mt-band" id="stt-t-rep"><span>Season repacker</span><b id="stt-rband"></b></div>
<div class="mt-box">
<div class="stt-lead"><p>Seasons downloaded episode by episode, replaced with the season pack through Sonarr; monitored series and seasons only, same or higher resolution, DV / HDR first. Nothing is deleted before the pack is complete and holds every episode you have; missing episodes (often the finale) come from the pack. With autobrr watched, new packs are listed here by themselves; the library scan tidies up what is already here.</p><span class="stt-leadact"><input type="text" id="stt-spq" list="stt-splist" autocomplete="off" placeholder="series name (empty = all)"> <input type="button" id="stt-spscan" value="Scan for season packs"></span></div>
<div class="stt-status"><span id="stt-spmsg"></span><span id="stt-abst"></span></div>
</div>
<datalist id="stt-splist"></datalist>
<div id="stt-spjobs"></div>
<div class="mt-box stt-splist"><div id="stt-spab"></div><div id="stt-spitems"></div></div>

<div class="stt-sethead" id="stt-t-set">Settings</div>
<form id="stt-form" onsubmit="return false;">
<div class="mt-band"><span>Connections</span><b>shared by the three tools</b></div>
<dl>
<dt>Prowlarr address and API key:</dt>
<dd><input type="text" name="prowlarr_url" placeholder="http://192.168.50.30:9696" style="width:260px"> <input type="password" name="prowlarr_key" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="API key" style="width:260px"></dd>
<dt>Radarr address and API key:</dt>
<dd><input type="text" name="radarr_url" placeholder="http://192.168.50.30:7878" style="width:260px"> <input type="password" name="radarr_key" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="API key" style="width:260px"></dd>
<dt>Sonarr address and API key:</dt>
<dd><input type="text" name="sonarr_url" placeholder="http://192.168.50.30:8989" style="width:260px"> <input type="password" name="sonarr_key" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="API key" style="width:260px"></dd>
<dt>Lidarr address and API key:</dt>
<dd><input type="text" name="lidarr_url" placeholder="http://192.168.50.30:8686" style="width:260px"> <input type="password" name="lidarr_key" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="API key" style="width:260px"> <span class="stt-hint">optional, for the Music folders (not used by the tools yet)</span></dd>
<dt>autobrr address and API key:</dt>
<dd><input type="text" name="autobrr_url" placeholder="http://192.168.50.30:7474" style="width:260px"> <input type="password" name="autobrr_key" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="API key" style="width:260px"> <span class="stt-hint">optional, only for the season pack messages of the Season repacker (autobrr, Settings, API keys)</span></dd>
<dt>Discord webhook:</dt>
<dd><input type="password" name="dc_hook" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="https://discord.com/api/webhooks/..." style="width:420px"> <span class="stt-hint">one webhook for all tools; each tool below has its own switch for sending messages. Type - to remove the saved webhook</span></dd>
<dt>Discord bot (reactions):</dt>
<dd><input type="password" name="bot_token" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="bot token" style="width:300px"> <input type="text" name="bot_user" placeholder="your Discord user ID" style="width:200px" inputmode="numeric">
<span class="stt-brk"></span><label><input type="checkbox" name="bot_rep" value="1"> season packs from autobrr</label> &nbsp; <label><input type="checkbox" name="bot_find" value="1"> torrents removed from the tracker (daily check)</label> &nbsp; <input type="button" id="stt-bottest" value="Test the bot" class="stt-ghost"> <span id="stt-botmsg" class="stt-mut"></span>
<span class="stt-hint">optional. The Seedbox message gets 1&#xFE0F;&#x20E3; 2&#xFE0F;&#x20E3; 3&#xFE0F;&#x20E3; &#x1F44E; reactions from your bot; a number starts that replacement (with the same checks as the button here), &#x1F44E; dismisses it. Only your reactions count, for 24 hours; the bot looks once a minute. Token: Discord Developer Portal, your app, Bot, Reset Token (leave empty to keep, - to remove). User ID: Discord, Settings, Advanced, Developer Mode, then right-click your name, Copy User ID. The bot needs View Channel, Add Reactions and Read Message History in the webhook's channel</span></dd>
<dt>Check the connections:</dt>
<dd><input type="button" id="stt-test" value="Test the connections"> <span class="stt-hint">tests the saved settings (Save first after a change): qBittorrent, the folder mapping, Discord (sends a test message), Prowlarr, Radarr, Sonarr, Lidarr, autobrr</span><div id="stt-tests" class="stt-mut"></div></dd>
<dt>Data folder, as qBittorrent sees it / on this server:</dt>
<dd><input type="text" name="map_qb" placeholder="/data" style="width:160px"> <input type="text" name="map_host" placeholder="/mnt/user/data" style="width:260px"></dd>
</dl>
<div class="mt-band"><span>Folders</span><b id="stt-foldband"></b></div>
<dl>
<dt>Downloads folder on this server:</dt>
<dd><input type="text" name="dl_base" placeholder="/mnt/user/data/downloads" style="width:320px;font-family:monospace"> <input type="button" id="stt-fread" class="stt-ghost" value="Read the folders again"><span class="stt-hint">every folder directly inside it is listed below with a role. A new folder shows up by itself as Other (marked new): Find my torrent sees it, Shape up and the Season repacker leave it alone until you change it. Save after a change.</span></dd>
</dl>
<div id="stt-folders"></div>
<div class="mt-band"><span>Scans and trash</span><b>shared by the three tools</b></div>
<dl>
<dt>Scheduled scan:</dt>
<dd><select name="auto_freq"><option value="daily">every day</option><option value="weekly">every week</option></select> <span class="stt-mut">(weekly: on</span> <select name="auto_day"><option value="1">Monday</option><option value="2">Tuesday</option><option value="3">Wednesday</option><option value="4">Thursday</option><option value="5">Friday</option><option value="6">Saturday</option><option value="7">Sunday</option></select><span class="stt-mut">)</span> at <input type="number" name="auto_hour" min="0" max="23" class="narrow"> :00
<span class="stt-brk"></span><label><input type="checkbox" name="auto_scan" value="1"> Find my torrent</label> &nbsp; <label><input type="checkbox" name="auto_upd" value="1"> Shape up</label> &nbsp; <label><input type="checkbox" name="auto_rep" value="1"> Season repacker</label>
<span class="stt-brk"></span><span class="stt-hint">the ticked tools scan one after the other at that time. Only scans run by themselves, nothing is added, replaced or deleted without your click. Torrents that a tracker removed are reported on Discord (if a webhook is saved, even when the other messages are off) and flagged in the Seedbox tile as <i>need attention</i></span></dd>
<dt>Replaced files stay in a trash folder for (days):</dt>
<dd><input type="number" name="trash_days" min="0" max="60" class="narrow"> <input type="button" id="stt-trempty" class="stt-ghost" value="Empty the trash now"> <span id="stt-trinfo" class="stt-mut"></span> <span class="stt-hint">0 = delete at once. The old folder is moved to <code>.seedbox_trash</code> inside its downloads folder and deleted after this many days</span></dd>
<dt>Dolby Vision on your TVs:</dt>
<dd><select name="dv_all"><option value="0">not every TV plays it</option><option value="1">every TV plays it</option></select> <span class="stt-hint">a Dolby Vision only release (DV without HDR10, mostly web releases) gives a purple and green picture on a TV without DV. With not every TV, such a release is never an upgrade and is marked; DV with HDR10 (DV+HDR) is the best. Changing it: Shape up, Forget results, search again</span></dd>
</dl>
<div class="mt-band"><span>Find my torrent</span><b></b></div>
<dl>
<dt>Find my torrent: accepted match (%):</dt>
<dd><input type="number" name="find_accept" min="90" max="100" step="0.5" class="narrow"> <span class="stt-hint">after the check, a torrent that matches at least this much of your files is started; qBittorrent downloads the missing rest (for example an .nfo file). Below it the torrent is removed again</span></dd>
<dt>Find my torrent: files that may be missing:</dt>
<dd><input type="number" name="find_missing_files" min="0" max="20" class="narrow"> <span class="stt-hint">if everything else matches and at most this many files of the torrent are missing from your folder, the torrent is started and qBittorrent downloads those files</span></dd>
<dt>Find my torrent: size tolerance (%):</dt>
<dd><input type="number" name="find_tol" min="0" max="10" step="0.5" class="narrow"> <span class="stt-hint">a torrent may be this much bigger than the folder (extra files such as .nfo)</span></dd>
<dt>Replace unseeded content: maximum size increase (%):</dt>
<dd><input type="number" name="repl_max_growth" min="0" max="1000" class="narrow"> <span class="stt-hint">a replacement may be at most this much bigger than what you have (0 = no limit). The same resolution and HDR format, closest in size, come first</span></dd>
<dt>Find my torrent: category:</dt>
<dd><label><input type="checkbox" name="find_cat" value="1"> give added torrents the category of Radarr / Sonarr</label> <span class="stt-hint">the category set in the qBittorrent download client of Radarr (movies) or Sonarr (series), by default it is radarr and sonarr respectively, you can change it in your Radarr or Sonarr instance under the download client setting. Torrents that match nothing will get the category most torrents in the same folder have</span></dd>
<dt>Widget tagline:</dt>
<dd><input type="text" name="tag_find" maxlength="60" placeholder="keeps your seed healthy 😉" style="width:320px"> <span class="stt-hint">the line under the tool name on the Dashboard tile; leave empty for the default</span></dd>
<dt>Show on the Dashboard:</dt>
<dd><select name="show_find"><option value="relevant">only when relevant</option><option value="always">always</option><option value="days">for N days after a scan</option><option value="never">never</option></select> <span class="stt-showd"><input type="number" name="show_find_days" min="1" max="60" class="narrow"> days</span> <span class="stt-hint">Relevant: something to fix, a scan running, never scanned. A failed or stuck row shows in every mode but never. When no row is left, the tools part of the tile is hidden.</span></dd>
<dt>Discord messages:</dt>
<dd><label><input type="checkbox" name="dc_find" value="1"> send them</label> <span class="stt-hint">off by default. The weekly check result (torrents removed by a tracker are always reported when a webhook is saved), and what happens to a replacement: started, imported, stuck, old files removed.</span></dd>
</dl>
<div class="mt-band"><span>Shape up</span><b>slimmer or stronger: a smaller release, a better HDR format or a higher resolution</b></div>
<dl>
<dt>Minimum size (GB), age (days), saving (%):</dt>
<dd><input type="number" name="upd_min_gb" min="1" max="1000" class="narrow"> <input type="number" name="upd_min_age" min="0" max="5000" class="narrow"> <input type="number" name="upd_saving" min="5" max="90" class="narrow"> <span class="stt-hint">titles at least this big and old are listed and searched in the background; a release counts as a saving if it is at least this much smaller</span></dd>
<dt>Offer:</dt>
<dd><label><input type="checkbox" name="upd_cat_save" value="1"> saving</label> &nbsp; <label><input type="checkbox" name="upd_cat_hdr" value="1"> HDR / DV upgrade</label> &nbsp; <label><input type="checkbox" name="upd_cat_res" value="1"> resolution upgrade</label> &nbsp; upgrades may be bigger by at most <input type="number" name="upd_upg_growth" min="0" max="1000" class="narrow"> % <span class="stt-hint">(0 = no limit). A release is never of a lower resolution or HDR format than what you have</span></dd>
<dt>Widget tagline:</dt>
<dd><input type="text" name="tag_upd" maxlength="60" placeholder="slimmer or stronger, in better shape" style="width:320px"> <span class="stt-hint">the line under the tool name on the Dashboard tile; leave empty for the default</span></dd>
<dt>Show on the Dashboard:</dt>
<dd><select name="show_upd"><option value="relevant">only when relevant</option><option value="always">always</option><option value="days">for N days after a scan</option><option value="never">never</option></select> <span class="stt-showd"><input type="number" name="show_upd_days" min="1" max="60" class="narrow"> days</span> <span class="stt-hint">Relevant: an offer, a scan or the background search running, never scanned. A failed or stuck row shows in every mode but never. When no row is left, the tools part of the tile is hidden.</span></dd>
<dt>Discord messages:</dt>
<dd><label><input type="checkbox" name="dc_upd" value="1"> send them</label> <span class="stt-hint">off by default. Replacement started, imported, stuck, old files removed.</span></dd>
</dl>
<div class="mt-band"><span>Season repacker</span><b>nothing to set: it works on the monitored series and seasons of Sonarr</b></div>
<dl>
<dt>Widget tagline:</dt>
<dd><input type="text" name="tag_rep" maxlength="60" placeholder="keeps your data tidy" style="width:320px"> <span class="stt-hint">the line under the tool name on the Dashboard tile; leave empty for the default</span></dd>
<dt>Show on the Dashboard:</dt>
<dd><select name="show_rep"><option value="relevant">only when relevant</option><option value="always">always</option><option value="days">for N days after a scan</option><option value="never">never</option></select> <span class="stt-showd"><input type="number" name="show_rep_days" min="1" max="60" class="narrow"> days</span> <span class="stt-hint">Relevant: a season that can be repacked, a repack or a scan running, never scanned. A failed or stuck row shows in every mode but never. When no row is left, the tools part of the tile is hidden.</span></dd>
<dt>Season packs from autobrr:</dt>
<dd><label><input type="checkbox" name="ab_on" value="1"> watch autobrr</label> <span class="stt-hint">every 5 minutes the releases that your autobrr filters let through are checked with Sonarr. A season pack of a monitored season that you have at least one episode of, not of a lower resolution (and Hungarian if your episodes are), is listed in the Season repacker under From autobrr and reported on Discord (with this switch, even when the messages below are off). Nothing is started</span><div id="stt-ab" class="stt-mut"></div></dd>
<dt>autobrr filters to use:</dt>
<dd><input type="hidden" name="ab_filters"><input type="button" id="stt-abf-load" value="Load filters"> <span id="stt-abf" class="stt-mut"></span> <span class="stt-hint">tick the filters whose releases are checked; none ticked = all filters. Then Save</span></dd>
<dt>Discord messages:</dt>
<dd><label><input type="checkbox" name="dc_rep" value="1"> send them</label> <span class="stt-hint">off by default. Season pack replacement started, done (with what was imported and trashed) or stuck.</span></dd>
</dl>
<dl>
<dt>&nbsp;</dt>
<dd><input type="button" id="stt-save" value="Save"> <span id="stt-cmsg" style="margin-left:10px"></span></dd>
</dl>
</form>
<?php $mt_lang_post = '/plugins/qbittorrent_widget/lang_save.php'; include '/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/qbittorrent_widget/lang_block.php'; ?>

</div>

<script>
$(function () {
  var lastSig = '', URL_ = '/plugins/qbittorrent_widget/tools.php', cfg = null, fT = null, uT = null, resT = {}, UPD = null, RES = {};
  function esc(s) { return $('<div>').text(s == null ? '' : String(s)).html(); }
  function fb(b) { b = +b; if (b >= 1e12) return (b / 1e12).toFixed(2) + ' TB'; if (b >= 1e9) return (b / 1e9).toFixed(b >= 1e11 ? 0 : 1) + ' GB'; return (b / 1e6).toFixed(0) + ' MB'; }
  function api(op, d) { return $.post(URL_, $.extend({op: op}, d || {}), null, 'json'); }
  function err(x) { return (x && x.responseJSON && x.responseJSON.error) ? x.responseJSON.error : (x && x.error) ? x.error : 'HTTP ' + (x && x.status); }
  function ago(t) { var s = Math.max(0, Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) - t); return s >= 86400 ? Math.floor(s / 86400) + ' d' : s >= 3600 ? Math.floor(s / 3600) + ' h' : Math.max(1, Math.floor(s / 60)) + ' m'; }

  // folder roles (Movies, Series, Music: the media library; Other: only Find my torrent; Not watched)
  var ROLES = [['movies', 'Movies', 's-green'], ['series', 'Series', 's-blue'], ['music', 'Music', 's-purple'], ['other', 'Other', 's-grey'], ['off', 'Not watched', 's-off']];
  var RNOTE = {movies: 'media library &middot; Radarr', series: 'media library &middot; Sonarr', music: 'media library &middot; no matching tool yet', other: 'seeding only (for example ratio torrents): only Find my torrent looks at it', off: 'no tool looks at it'};
  function roleTools(r) { return [r !== 'off', r === 'movies' || r === 'series', r === 'series']; }
  function folderRow(n, f) {
    var o = ''; $.each(ROLES, function (i, x) { o += '<option value="' + x[0] + '"' + (x[0] === f.role ? ' selected' : '') + '>' + x[1] + '</option>'; });
    return '<div class="stt-fr" data-n="' + esc(n) + '"><span><b>' + esc(n) + '</b>' + (f['new'] ? '<span class="stt-badge a">new</span>' : '') + '<small class="stt-fnote"></small></span><span><select class="stt-frole" aria-label="Role of ' + esc(n) + '">' + o + '</select></span><span class="stt-ft"></span><span class="stt-ft"></span><span class="stt-ft"></span></div>';
  }
  function folderPaint() {
    var w = 0, lib = 0, nw = $('#stt-folders .stt-badge').length;
    $('#stt-folders .stt-fr[data-n]').each(function () {
      var r = $(this).find('.stt-frole').val(), t = roleTools(r), cls = $.grep(ROLES, function (x) { return x[0] === r; })[0][2];
      $(this).removeClass('s-green s-blue s-purple s-grey s-off s-amber').addClass($(this).find('.stt-badge').length ? 's-amber' : cls);
      $(this).find('.stt-fnote').html(RNOTE[r]);
      $(this).find('.stt-ft').each(function (i) { $(this).toggleClass('y', t[i]).html(t[i] ? '&#10003;' : '&ndash;'); });
      if (r !== 'off') { w++; } if (r === 'movies' || r === 'series' || r === 'music') { lib++; }
    });
    $('#stt-foldband').text(w + ' watched · ' + lib + ' media library' + (nw ? ' · ' + nw + ' new' : ''));
  }
  function drawFolders(list) {
    var h = '<div class="stt-fr stt-fh"><span>Folder</span><span>Role</span><span>Find my torrent</span><span>Shape up</span><span>Season repacker</span></div>', n = 0;
    // most tools first: Series, Movies, Music, Other, Not watched; by name inside a role (sorted when drawn, not while you change a role)
    var RK = {series: 0, movies: 1, music: 2, other: 3, off: 4};
    $.each(Object.keys(list).sort(function (a, b) { return (RK[list[a].role] - RK[list[b].role]) || a.localeCompare(b, undefined, {sensitivity: 'base', numeric: true}); }), function (i, k) { h += folderRow(k, list[k]); n++; });
    if (!n) { h += '<div class="stt-fr"><span class="stt-mut">No folder found inside the downloads folder (is the array started, is the path right?)</span></div>'; }
    $('#stt-folders').html(h); folderPaint();
  }
  $(document).on('change', '.stt-frole', function () { $(this).closest('.stt-fr').find('.stt-badge').remove(); folderPaint(); });
  $(document).on('click', '#stt-fread', function () {
    var $b = $(this).prop('disabled', true);
    api('folders', {dl_base: $('#stt-form [name=dl_base]').val()}).done(function (r) { if (r.ok) { drawFolders(r.folder_list || {}); } else { window.alert(r.error); } })
      .fail(function (x) { window.alert(err(x)); }).always(function () { $b.prop('disabled', false); });
  });
